**Effective Date: October 26, 2026**

Welcome to Savepoint!

Savepoint is a creative journaling app that transforms everyday photos into game-inspired save files. We value your privacy and are committed to protecting your personal information.

This Privacy Policy explains how Savepoint uses device permissions, processes your creative content, and allows you to manage your information.

## 1. How We Handle Your Information

Savepoint does not require you to create an account or log in to use the app.

The app's main features include taking photos, importing images, adding game-inspired elements, editing text, and creating game save files.

To provide these features, we may need access to the following information and device permissions:

### 1.1 Camera Access

When you use the camera feature, Savepoint will request permission to access your device's camera.

This permission is used solely for taking photos. We will not capture photos or videos without your explicit action.

### 1.2 Photo Library Access

When you choose to import photos or save your creations to your device's photo library, Savepoint may request the necessary permissions.

We only access or save photos when you actively use these features. We do not automatically scan your entire photo library.

### 1.3 User-Generated Content

Content you create in Savepoint may include photos, written entries, game element configurations, and game save files.

All such content is stored locally on your device and is used solely to support editing, managing, and viewing your creations.

We do not automatically upload this content to developer-operated servers or use it for advertising or marketing purposes.

## 2. Data Storage and Security

Savepoint stores your creative content locally on your device and does not provide a developer-operated cloud synchronization service.

Your photos, written entries, and game save files are stored and managed on your device.

Locally stored content generally remains on your device until you choose to delete it or remove the app's data.

Please note:

- You can manage and delete your game save files using the features available within the app.
- Uninstalling the app may result in the loss of app data that has not been backed up.
- Images saved to your device's photo library are not affected when you delete content within Savepoint. You must manage these images separately in your photo library.
- If you have enabled system backup services, some app data may be processed by your device's backup provider in accordance with its privacy policy.

We recommend keeping your device secure and regularly backing up important creations.

## 3. In-App Purchases

Savepoint may introduce in-app purchases or subscription services in the future to unlock additional assets and premium features.

These paid services are not currently available in the app.

If paid features are introduced, transactions will be processed through Apple's in-app purchase system.

Savepoint does not directly collect or store your full payment card details or other complete payment information.

We will update this Privacy Policy as necessary to reflect the payment features implemented and their associated data processing practices.

## 4. Third-Party Services

Savepoint may use basic operating system features to enable camera access, photo library access, and other essential app functionality.

If we introduce third-party analytics, crash reporting, or other services that process personal information, we will review their data processing practices before implementation.

We will disclose the relevant service providers, purposes of processing, types of information involved, and methods of data sharing as required by applicable laws. Where legally required, we will obtain your consent.

We do not sell your personal photos, written entries, or other creative content.

## 5. Your Rights and Choices

You can manage your information in the following ways:

### 5.1 Managing Device Permissions

You can disable Savepoint's access to your camera or photo library at any time through your device's iOS Settings.

Disabling these permissions may affect the availability of certain features.

### 5.2 Managing Your Content

You can view, edit, or delete locally stored game save files using the features available within the app.

### 5.3 Withdrawing Consent

You can withdraw permissions previously granted to Savepoint at any time through your device's system settings.

### 5.4 Contacting Us

If you have questions about how your personal information is processed or wish to exercise your rights to access, correct, or delete personal information under applicable laws, you may contact us using the information provided in this Privacy Policy.

We will handle your requests in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.

## 6. Children's Privacy

Savepoint is committed to protecting the privacy and personal information of minors.

If you are under the age of 14, please review this Privacy Policy with a parent or legal guardian and obtain their consent before using the app.

Our services are not designed for the purpose of collecting personal information from minors.

If our operations involve personal information belonging to minors that requires special protection under applicable laws, we will implement appropriate safeguards and fulfill the relevant legal obligations.

## 7. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time as Savepoint's features and services evolve.

If any updates involve significant changes to how personal information is processed, we will notify you through appropriate channels and obtain your consent again where required by law.

The latest version of this Privacy Policy will be published on a publicly accessible page, along with its effective date.

